[7.337747, "o", "cat /root/material_density_table.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[7.338707, "o", "# Proprietary Material Density Table\r\n\r\nThis table lists the density values for the proprietary materials used in the Constructo-95 system.\r\nUse the Material ID found in the CAD file attributes to lookup the corresponding density.\r\n\r\n| Material ID | Material Name | Density (g/cm³) | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| **1** | Generic Debris | 0.10 | Low-density dust/noise artifacts. |\r\n| **10** | Standard Steel | 7.85 | Common structural steel. |\r\n| **25** | Aluminum 6061 | 2.70 | Aerospace grade aluminum. |\r\n| **42** | Unobtanium | 5.55 | High-strength proprietary alloy. |\r\n| **99** | Lead | 11.34 | Heavy ballast material. |\r\n\r\n## Formula\r\n\r\n$$ Mass = Volume \\times Density $$\r\n\r\nNote: Ensure volume is in $cm^3$ and density is in $g/cm^3$.\r\n"]
[7.338878, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@1d410785f904:~# "]
[18.712552, "i", "python3 << 'EOF'\nimport struct\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\nimport json\n\n# Parse binary STL\nwith open('/root/scan_data.stl', 'rb') as f:\n    header = f.read(80)\n    num_triangles = struct.unpack('<I', f.read(4))[0]\n    print(f\"Number of triangles: {num_triangles}\")\n    \n    triangles = []\n    material_ids = []\n    \n    for i in range(num_triangles):\n        # Normal vector (3 floats)\n        normal = struct.unpack('<3f', f.read(12))\n        # 3 vertices (3 floats each)\n        v1 = struct.unpack('<3f', f.read(12))\n        v2 = struct.unpack('<3f', f.read(12))\n        v3 = struct.unpack('<3f', f.read(12))\n        # Attribute byte count (2 bytes) - contains Material ID\n        material_id = struct.unpack('<H', f.read(2))[0]\n        \n        triangles.append((v1, v2, v3))\n        material_ids.append(material_id)\n\nprint(f\"Unique material IDs: {set(material_ids)}\")\nprint(f\"Material ID counts: {dict((mid, material_ids.count(mid)) for mid in set(material_ids))}\")\n\nEOF\n"]
